body:
/start lists what it takes to earn, in order, and reads each step instead of
remembering it:
1. the wallet, from the session;
2. gas, or a sponsor, from the balance or the sponsorship;
3. the passkey, from PasskeyRegistry on chain;
4. a drive at the station, from this browser;
5. the first paid run, from the ledger.
Only the next step offers its action. The landing's primary button and the
Earn menu now lead there, and the live journey checks a fresh wallet goes
from 0/5 to 5/5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

CI used Foundry's newest release (1.8.5). It counts gas differently from the
1.7.1 the snapshot was taken with: every external call cost about 21k more,
so forge snapshot --check failed everywhere. Its forge script also timed out
against anvil when deploying the local chain. Both jobs now pin v1.7.1, the
version the suite and the snapshot were made with.

docs/screens: seven key screens at 1440x900 and 390x844, captured from the
local stack with real signed state by scripts/capture-screens.mjs:
- landing;
- the station mid-drive;
- a paid run;
- an x402 corpus purchase;
- the leaderboard;
- the passkey's derived SO-101 key;
- agents.
scripts/contact-sheet.py lays them out as two sheets, which the README now
shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

verify.yml had failed on every run since the move to pnpm:
- npm ci found no package-lock;
- forge test found no forge-std (contracts/lib is ignored, not vendored);
- the live job ran before installing anything.

Now:
- static: pnpm, tsc, eslint over the repo, the unit suite, the model check;
- contracts: forge-std v1.16.2 installed, forge test, the gas snapshot
  (re-snapshotted on purpose; it dated from 12 Sep), forge lint;
- localnet, new: anvil with the contracts DeployMonad.s.sol deploys, the
  local x402 facilitator, the app built and served against them, then
  every page and API (pnpm test:e2e:local) with real transactions behind;
- live, on the schedule: the read-only e2e against https://thenar.io,
  which passes. The itemised qa-* suite assumes paid runs on the Monad
  deployment, so it runs on demand until the testnet go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
